course: dictionary
lesson: 8089
title: Remember and what it means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To remember means to keep something in your mind and bring it back later. «I remember my first day at school» means the day is still in my mind, so I can think about it now.
explain: Remember can also mean not to forget to do something. «Remember to bring your hat» is a reminder: the hat must stay in your mind before you leave the house. Look at the words after remember to see which meaning the writer means.
explain: Remember can also mean to keep a day or an event in mind, so people do not forget it. Ask yourself what the word would fit here, then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Remember is a verb: remember, remembers, remembered, remembering.
fact: «Remember» can mean to keep something in your mind: «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle, and dolphins remember old friends' whistles for over 20 years.»
fact: «Remember» can mean not to forget to do something: «Remember to bring your hat.»
fact: «Remember» can mean to keep a date or event in mind: «It remembers 14 July 1789, when people in Paris took the Bastille, a prison fortress.»
fact: A good check is to swap in «do not forget» or «keep in mind» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «I remember my first day at school.» What does remember mean here? | *To keep it in your mind and think back to it | To buy something new | To fall asleep | To shout loudly
exercise: «Remember to bring your hat.» What does remember mean here? | To lose your hat | To count to ten | *To not forget to do it | To put a hat on your head and sleep in it
exercise: «Each bottlenose dolphin remembers old friends' whistles for over 20 years.» How long do dolphins remember the whistles of old friends? | Over 2 hours | Over 20 days | Over 2 weeks | *Over 20 years
test: «It remembers 14 July 1789, when people in Paris took the Bastille.» In this sentence, remember means: | To build a fortress | To paint a picture of Paris | To forget a date | *To keep a date and event in mind
test: Mia says, «Remember your address, in case you get lost.» Why is it important to remember your address? | *So you can tell someone where you live if you need help | So you can sing it in a song | It makes your bag heavier | It helps you tell the time
exam: In «Remember to bring your hat», which phrase could replace remember without changing the meaning? | Throw away | *Do not forget | Be sad about | Be quiet about
